 "caveats": [
  "Payment-year mapping is approximate: star year Y determines QBP status for payment year CY(Y+1); star-2026 contracts pay in CY2027, which has no enrollment data yet, so the July 2026 snapshot is a proxy. Star-2025 (CY2026 payment) and star-2024 (CY2025 payment) contracts use in-payment-year months (2026-07 and 2025-12).",
  "Enrollment is a single monthly snapshot; enrollment moves over the payment year (and star-driven marketing effects themselves move it), so annualizing one month misstates member-months.",
  "County double-bonus variation not modeled: the benchmark bonus is 5% in most counties, 10% in double-bonus counties; the mix varies by contract.",
  "Rebate interactions not modeled: the 3.5->4.0 crossing mainly changes the benchmark bonus (rebate share is 65% on both sides of 4.0), but bonus-inflated benchmarks raise rebates for bidding plans, an effect included differently across the public reference figures.",
  "Per-enrollee QBP value varies with plan mix (SNP vs individual vs employer), county benchmarks, and bids; the $400-$600 band brackets the public per-enrollee averages, not this specific set's plan mix.",
  "Enrollment joined at contract level (all plans under the contract), matching the level at which the overall star rating and QBP status attach for MA-PD locals."
 ]
}